{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs6WmgYBbeUQXNR9QPgr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The sitting is done in three commits: the verdict (`7262a56d`), the amendment re-attestation (`51ce7b2a`), and the approval act (`99840c32`). All carry the `WI: WI-834` trailer and passed the commit hooks. Several rows I approved on merit could not be flipped yet. LLR-300 is the single row holding them.\n\n**amendment: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=9`.** Every row adds a blackout case its old text lacked. I would bless eight of the nine, but not LLR-300:\n- Its new hook-denial clause traces only to SR-229, which governs claim admission. Denying model launches is SR-237's \"pause new model work\", and the spine-authoring rule forbids tracing a clause to a parent whose text doesn't demand it.\n- Its detail never states the close-down instruction the hooks inject, so no spine row carries that delivered behaviour.\n\nI tried the LLR re-attestation to confirm, and the copy was refused, naming only `LLR-300: Detail`. So:\n- **Re-attested:** SR-227, SR-229, SR-230, TC-267, TC-317, TC-318.\n- **Blessed but still unanchored:** LLR-270 and LLR-301. They anchor once LLR-300 is fixed.\n- **One draft for LLR-300:** add SR-237 to its parents, state the close-down instruction, and cite three tests no TC cites. No code change.\n\n**first-approval: `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=13`** (8 approve, 5 return).\n- **Approved:** SR-237, LLR-316, LLR-317, LLR-318, LLR-319, TC-335, TC-338, TC-340.\n  - Flipped: SR-237 and TC-340 only.\n  - Not flipped: LLR-316 to LLR-319, because flipping them needs the same blocked LLR registry copy. TC-335 and TC-338 wait on their parents, LLR-316 and LLR-319.\n- **Returned, with three drafts:**\n  - **TC-339:** it verifies LLR-300, which isn't blessed, and it lacks SR-237.\n  - **TC-341:** it lacks SR-237, so SR-237's retention clause has no verifying TC, and it doesn't state its in-window cases.\n  - **TC-336:** no test checks LLR-317's lease release on refusal. The arms map marks this covered, but no test passes a retained session into a refused call.\n  - **TC-337:** its tests drive only the helper. Removing the retry from any of LLR-318's three loop call sites would pass every cited test.\n  - **TC-342:** no LLR states the bare-run readiness check. The approved LLR-047 still calls the `run.*` launchers \"thin delegates\", which they no longer are. Parts C and D also have ten tests that no TC cites.\n\n**done-when: `DONE-WHEN: BLESSED changes=2`.** The swapped test bullet counts as two changes: one dropped, one added. The scope narrowed: the old bullet promised a check of the handoff's contents, the new one checks the pinned close-down instruction plus refusal inside the window and admission after it. This is exactly the remedy from my earlier ruling on the R2F2 dispute, and the work item's purpose still holds.\n\nThe `.requested` marker is left untracked for the coordinator."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":282,"cache_read_input_tokens":247279,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":282},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d8d1fbc-6a42-4a02-9ec0-8f8d2b61c24c","uuid":"8ce26d02-20f9-4d39-b321-de28fccac75c","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:57:35.969Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs6WmQRqMb9pX6SHdeFV"}
